WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Hold a light weight on a thread. Imagine it swinging.
Sometimes it starts to move, even when your hand feels still.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A convincing experience is not yet proof
of the first explanation that comes to mind.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
In the 1970s, researchers changed what people
could see and hear as they held pendulums.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Visual feedback mattered.
Delayed feedback could disrupt the movement.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Keep three things apart: motion, the feeling of control,
and claims of hidden knowledge.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Before buying a mind-training audio,
ask the same question: what was actually measured?
